   "guide": "CO2 at 10–14 mmHg is the standard distension medium with nitrous oxide as backup, while air and oxygen are banned for supporting combustion. Peritoneal stretch vagally slows the heart into sinus bradycardia, IVC compression drops venous return and cardiac output with early bradycardia then hypotension and reflex tachycardia, the raised diaphragm shrinks thoracic volume and raises airway resistance and intrathoracic pressure needing extra PEEP in COPD, renal vessel pressure cuts urine output, and intracranial tension rises."
